1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:04,150
The world has fallen in love

2
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:07,820
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:11,110
I just want to understand you

4
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:15,490
Won't you open up to me?

5
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:26,630
A fumbled exchange of words leaves a little taste of regret

6
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,960
Enough to make me cry

7
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:35,300
I want to link my racing emotions to the beat of my heart

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,430
and put it all in tune

9
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,270
I lost sight of everything but my goal

10
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:51,940
and had something important fade away

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:58,200
Let's start all over

12
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:03,330
The world has fallen in love

13
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:06,580
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

14
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:10,170
I want to know everything about you

15
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:14,340
Won't you tell me more?

16
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:17,970
One inch feels like a million miles

17
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:20,890
as the days just seem to race by

18
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:25,310
I won't and can't ever forget

19
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:28,560
this brightest page of my life.

20
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:34,680
I was so desperate that I lost sight of everything but my goal.

21
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,740
About your mother's condition...

22
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:50,150
If I may, are you her only family?

23
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:52,390
My parents are divorced.

24
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:56,550
My brother and father both live far away.

25
00:01:56,550 --> 00:02:01,300
Then please get me in touch with one of them.

26
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:05,430
I'm the only family that can be here with her.

27
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,890
She doesn't have any other relatives?

28
00:02:12,710 --> 00:02:15,530
No, it's just me.

29
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:24,460
I'm the only one who can be there for her right now.

30
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:39,550
Oh, Kou.

31
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:41,900
What did the doctor say?

32
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:46,800
They'll need to do a few more tests to be sure.

33
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:49,590
Just gotta wait and see, I guess.

34
00:02:49,590 --> 00:02:51,020
Okay.

35
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:53,130
How does your back feel?

36
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:55,330
It's a lot better now.

37
00:02:55,330 --> 00:02:57,740
The painkillers must be working.

38
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,700
Wonder if it's a hernia.

39
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:04,150
I never knew they were supposed to hurt so much.

40
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:06,470
Goodness, what am I to do?

41
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:14,330
Kou.

42
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:19,660
I'll be fine here, so head on home.

43
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:25,970
I think I'm coming down with a cold, and I wouldn't want to get you sick.

44
00:03:29,090 --> 00:03:31,730
Just a little longer couldn't...

45
00:03:37,190 --> 00:03:41,280
Alright, I guess I'll go. I need to pick you up some things for your stay, too.

46
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:43,250
I'll go for today.

47
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,990
See you tomorrow.

48
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,910
See you then.

49
00:03:57,450 --> 00:04:00,670
Your mother has lung cancer.

50
00:04:01,570 --> 00:04:04,620
Her back pain implies that it's also metastasized to her bones.

51
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:07,260
From this...

52
00:04:12,970 --> 00:04:17,780
It's fine. I was able to act like usual around her.

53
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:35,370
Hello, Youichi? It's Mom.

54
00:04:35,770 --> 00:04:40,130
Sorry, Youichi. It looks like...

55
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:44,350
...I may not have much longer.

56
00:04:45,770 --> 00:04:49,990
Kou is trying his hardest to act like nothing's wrong.

57
00:04:51,670 --> 00:04:53,240
Yes, you're right.

58
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:57,690
I'll speak to the doctor about it.

59
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:00,300
Youichi.

60
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:04,150
Please take care of Kou for me.

61
00:05:10,650 --> 00:05:14,900
From this, the cancer appears to be in its terminal stages.

62
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:17,890
To be honest, there is no effective treatment.

63
00:05:21,770 --> 00:05:25,940
Your mother has half a year left, at best.

64
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:29,750
Could...

65
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:34,560
Could I have saved her if I'd realized it sooner?

66
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:38,350
I wanted to put her mind at ease about the future,

67
00:05:38,350 --> 00:05:42,990
so I spent almost all my free time studying

68
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:47,390
to get into good high schools, colleges, and companies.

69
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:54,580
Kou, dinner's ready.

70
00:05:55,470 --> 00:05:59,160
I'm not at a good stopping point yet, so eat without me.

71
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:02,090
What, again?

72
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:05,850
You're making Mom lonely.

73
00:06:05,850 --> 00:06:08,010
What are you saying?

74
00:06:08,010 --> 00:06:13,600
You say that now, but you'll be thanking me once I get my first paycheck.

75
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:18,600
I'm not too concerned about that.

76
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:24,410
Eating dinner or watching TV together is a lot more important to me.

77
00:06:33,570 --> 00:06:34,640
Mom...

78
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:40,350
I...

79
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:44,390
...made a mistake.

80
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,650
I'm sorry...

81
00:06:52,650 --> 00:06:56,400
I was so desperate, I lost sight of everything but my goal.

82
00:06:57,530 --> 00:06:59,950
But that was a mistake.

83
00:07:01,730 --> 00:07:04,770
I should've focused on what was really important.

84
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:09,030
But it's too late now.

85
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:30,970
No one is available to answer at this time.

86
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:36,450
Please leave your name and a short message after the beep.

87
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:41,980
Tanaka Kouichi

88
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:41,980
Hey, it's your brother...

89
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:44,780
Kou, are you there?

90
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:49,810
I just heard from Mom.

91
00:07:51,980 --> 00:07:55,090
Kou, I'm leaving Mom in your hands.

92
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,890
I'm s-sorry...

93
00:08:06,890 --> 00:08:08,120
Sorry...

94
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,470
I'm sorry.

95
00:08:11,970 --> 00:08:13,470
I'm sorry!

96
00:08:14,430 --> 00:08:15,830
I'm so sorry!

97
00:08:16,890 --> 00:08:18,710
I'm sorry!

98
00:08:18,710 --> 00:08:19,860
Kou!

99
00:08:23,630 --> 00:08:25,310
Kou!

100
00:08:26,750 --> 00:08:29,810
Yoshioka? Oh yeah...

101
00:08:29,810 --> 00:08:32,070
Are we playing cops and robbers?

102
00:08:32,810 --> 00:08:36,570
Man, that's a heck of a face she's running over with.

103
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,610
My neck kills...

104
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:51,340
Don't get stuck doing
extra lessons all summer!
Futaba

105
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:51,340
You can do it, Kou
Finish all this and
you'll be OK
Aya

106
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:21,760
Hey, Kou.

107
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:24,320
Kou?

108
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:28,110
What're you spacing out for?

109
00:09:28,110 --> 00:09:29,850
C'mon, let's go.

110
00:09:31,490 --> 00:09:33,960
We know you don't have work today.

111
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:37,180
That means you can study all we want.

112
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:42,600
Library

113
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:44,080
Here we go! Here we go!

114
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:47,560
Mabuchi-kun, what subject do you want to start with?

115
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:51,020
Whatever you want.

116
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:56,070
I'll take that to mean that you're open to anything.

117
00:09:56,070 --> 00:09:59,990
Oh, right, I brought the latest in my math notes series.

118
00:10:00,370 --> 00:10:01,080
Chemistry

119
00:10:00,370 --> 00:10:01,080
Review

120
00:10:00,490 --> 00:10:02,800
I made a chemistry one for you, too.

121
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:16,010
I'm gonna go to the bathroom before we start.

122
00:10:16,010 --> 00:10:18,620
Sure thing, see ya.

123
00:10:29,150 --> 00:10:31,350
Mabuchi-kun's been gone for a while.

124
00:10:33,310 --> 00:10:35,150
What's he doing in there?

125
00:10:36,180 --> 00:10:39,070
Didn't he just go home?

126
00:10:39,070 --> 00:10:40,310
What?

127
00:10:40,310 --> 00:10:43,270
Come on, he's probably just taking a big one.

128
00:10:43,270 --> 00:10:45,270
So why's his bag gone?

129
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:46,950
Is it really?

130
00:10:50,530 --> 00:10:52,050
He tricked us!

131
00:10:52,050 --> 00:10:54,150
I knew he was a brat.

132
00:10:54,150 --> 00:10:56,340
You won't get away!

133
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:57,830
Let's go!

134
00:10:57,830 --> 00:11:01,110
If we leave now, we can still catch him!

135
00:11:03,430 --> 00:11:04,260
Ah, sor—

136
00:11:08,470 --> 00:11:09,800
S-Sorry abou—

137
00:11:10,690 --> 00:11:15,150
Self-restraint

138
00:11:15,150 --> 00:11:17,360
Ahhhh!

139
00:11:17,670 --> 00:11:19,650
I'm so sorry!

140
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:21,320
Wait, Futaba-chan!

141
00:11:23,310 --> 00:11:25,370
Why is this happening?!

142
00:11:27,610 --> 00:11:29,010
What an unfortunate accident.

143
00:11:29,570 --> 00:11:31,790
A bit too unfortunate.

144
00:11:32,580 --> 00:11:35,750
Damn, he got away.

145
00:11:36,650 --> 00:11:40,600
He seemed really out of it today.

146
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,970
Yeah, there was something strange about him.

147
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:46,260
Can't figure the guy out.

148
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:50,630
Don't you get the feeling he's keeping something big to himself?

149
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:58,240
Just when I thought we were getting closer to him, he pushes us away again.

150
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:01,080
He's just like a cat.

151
00:12:03,770 --> 00:12:05,120
Sounds about right.

152
00:12:05,460 --> 00:12:09,940
He probably doesn't even know what he wants. He's not the brightest.

153
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:12,580
Still, I can't help but like him.

154
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:18,110
I'm gonna drag him around all summer vacation.

155
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:21,260
I'd love for us all to go somewhere together.

156
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:24,340
Like the movies, or an amusement park...

157
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:28,470
Oh! We could go hiking again like during the leadership course!

158
00:12:28,870 --> 00:12:31,920
Sure, as long as we don't get lost again.

159
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:36,640
Oh, well... that time, um...

160
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:39,400
Kou, we're all waiting for you.

161
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:45,760
It's a bright and cheerful world right outside your door.

162
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:50,080
Why won't you come out?

163
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:52,750
Come out! Get out here, Kou!

164
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:54,290
We're all waiting!

165
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,970
Oh, Tanaka-sensei.

166
00:13:02,970 --> 00:13:05,930
If you're looking for Kou, he's not back yet.

167
00:13:06,470 --> 00:13:11,030
Sensei, Kou-kun won't open the door to his heart!

168
00:13:11,890 --> 00:13:15,350
He keeps opening all these other doors to me,

169
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:20,440
but the one I really want opened is locked tight.

170
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:23,660
Behind a double lock, even.

171
00:13:25,270 --> 00:13:29,410
Is that so? I think you're a bit off, though.

172
00:13:30,870 --> 00:13:33,230
If we're going to go with your metaphor,

173
00:13:33,230 --> 00:13:38,170
it's more like he didn't even give the door a doorknob, never mind a lock.

174
00:13:38,170 --> 00:13:40,630
What?
Then he's just an idiot...

175
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:45,480
Sensei, what should I do now?

176
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:48,090
Onii-chan doesn't have a clue either.

177
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:55,980
Then I'll just have to smash that door to pieces!

178
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:57,730
Mabuchi

179
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:57,730
Tanaka

180
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,540
That damn brat!

181
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:04,370
Just like how Kou opened the door to my heart, I can open his!

182
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:12,370
She's like a storm.

183
00:14:25,010 --> 00:14:28,420
Kou, it's time to come out.

184
00:14:29,780 --> 00:14:31,290
Open your door.

185
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:05,550
He's here! He's really here!

186
00:15:08,130 --> 00:15:10,590
You know what they did next?

187
00:15:11,430 --> 00:15:12,590
Seriously?

188
00:15:14,390 --> 00:15:18,060
If you want someone to talk with, then I'm right here.

189
00:15:20,810 --> 00:15:24,310
A-And Kominato-kun and Yuuri are, too.

190
00:15:24,310 --> 00:15:25,400
Kou.

191
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:27,610
Hey, Kou!

192
00:15:27,610 --> 00:15:31,160
Are we too boring for you or something?

193
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:32,740
Sorry, man.

194
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:37,160
Nah, don't worry. That's just what Kou's like.

195
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:39,200
He's always like this.

196
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,580
For real?

197
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:44,170
Actually, you haven't been around much lately.

198
00:15:44,170 --> 00:15:47,380
Got something nice in your life?

199
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:55,680
No, not really.

200
00:15:56,220 --> 00:15:57,720
Kou!

201
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:13,200
Again she comes running, with that dumb look on her face.

202
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:24,370
I told you not to go there by yourself.

203
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:32,550
Kou, how long are you going to keep this up?

204
00:16:32,550 --> 00:16:34,930
Keep what up?

205
00:16:34,930 --> 00:16:40,140
Keep everything up! Everything you're doing right now.

206
00:16:55,780 --> 00:16:59,240
Doesn't it tire you out?

207
00:16:59,910 --> 00:17:02,040
What's the point of it?

208
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:08,790
There is no point.

209
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:14,260
Nothing I do has a point.

210
00:17:15,090 --> 00:17:18,220
You probably can't understand with your "start over from step one" attitude.

211
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:22,640
I know that...

212
00:17:24,350 --> 00:17:26,140
But if she saw you like this,

213
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:30,480
I'm sure your mother would be sad—

214
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:32,110
You don't need to tell me.

215
00:17:32,110 --> 00:17:34,990
The thought of it tortures me day and night.

216
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:41,200
But that kind of thinking won't solve anything.

217
00:17:43,330 --> 00:17:48,380
Even if I realized all the mistakes I've made, I can't do it over.

218
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:55,420
I watched my mother grow thinner by the day

219
00:17:55,420 --> 00:17:59,890
as she resigned herself to her fate.

220
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:04,020
What I felt back then...

221
00:18:05,810 --> 00:18:11,230
...you will never understand.

222
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:17,400
But you know, sometimes things just don't go your way.

223
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:20,490
That's when you go back to step one.

224
00:18:20,490 --> 00:18:22,370
And there's nothing wrong with that.

225
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,200
I'm glad.

226
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:35,340
Kou is suffering as much now as he did then.

227
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:41,140
No one but Kou himself will ever fully understand his feelings.

228
00:18:42,850 --> 00:18:44,560
No matter how hard I try,

229
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,100
it'll never be enough.

230
00:18:48,310 --> 00:18:49,440
But still...

231
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:52,940
But still!

232
00:18:56,740 --> 00:18:59,660
I want to understand you with all of my heart.

233
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:03,120
Is that really so wrong?

234
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:09,670
I just want to smash it to pieces.

235
00:19:10,330 --> 00:19:14,460
I want to smash that damned door to bits!

236
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,720
Why...

237
00:19:26,890 --> 00:19:30,480
Why are you trying to hard to break in?

238
00:19:30,980 --> 00:19:33,610
Not just you. Everyone.

239
00:19:39,490 --> 00:19:42,200
I'm scared of that.

240
00:19:43,490 --> 00:19:44,450
Kou!

241
00:19:44,450 --> 00:19:46,240
Hey, wait! Sto—

242
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:56,460
Th-That was terrifying.

243
00:19:57,340 --> 00:19:58,630
She's heavy...

244
00:20:02,050 --> 00:20:03,680
It's too late!

245
00:20:05,350 --> 00:20:11,310
If you feel scared, then that means you already see us as precious!

246
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:15,270
You're scared to lose us, aren't you?

247
00:20:18,070 --> 00:20:21,360
You really know how to be annoying.

248
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:27,240
If you've lost so much already that no one thing can ever replace it,

249
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:30,830
you just have to grab as much as you can.

250
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:36,670
They might be so small that it takes tens or hundreds of them, but when you've found enough...

251
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:42,090
...you'll finally want to live again!

252
00:20:43,970 --> 00:20:49,890
It's perfectly fine to get too into something or to laugh like an idiot.

253
00:20:49,890 --> 00:20:53,940
And if anyone says otherwise, I'll beat them up!

254
00:21:06,450 --> 00:21:09,200
Oh... she's right...

255
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:11,580
All I wanted...

256
00:21:12,410 --> 00:21:16,630
...was to be able to live and laugh freely.

257
00:21:17,250 --> 00:21:20,090
Someone to tell me it was okay...

258
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:23,130
...to have meaning in my life.

259
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:43,400
I really have been...

260
00:21:44,650 --> 00:21:49,700
...waiting for a storm like her to come.

261
00:22:00,630 --> 00:22:05,760
In a town beset by a sudden shower,

262
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:11,140
I say "See you later", and wave goodbye.

263
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:16,600
As I watch you pass through the ticket gate, I think:

264
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:21,900
"It never goes according to plan, does it?"

265
00:22:21,900 --> 00:22:31,620
Everything seemed incredibly fragile that day,

266
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:37,210
but it passed, as days tend to do.

267
00:22:38,370 --> 00:22:47,760
The rails carry you away

268
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:56,020
leaving me alone on our usual path.

269
00:22:57,140 --> 00:23:06,650
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

270
00:23:06,650 --> 00:23:15,370
so why can't I say them?

271
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:22,330
Why can't I?

272
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:39,890
NEXT TIME...

273
00:23:27,210 --> 00:23:28,050
See you tomorrow!

274
00:23:28,550 --> 00:23:30,380
Yeah, see you at school.

275
00:23:30,380 --> 00:23:32,510
Yep, see you!

276
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:34,140
Yoshioka.

277
00:23:35,390 --> 00:23:36,510
Thanks.

278
00:23:38,680 --> 00:23:39,850
Yeah!
